  "resident_configuration_change": "Agents adds AISOC_TRIAGE_KB_KEYS_FILE and dedicated read-only UID10001 directory; organisation-memory and skill identities/env/mounts preserved. No shared token fallback.",
  "authentication_contract": "Only internal runbooks/for-triage GET changes to standard Bearer knowledge_base:read with tenant intersection and RLS. Other query/ingest/delete paths retain existing permissions; Agents chooses dedicated per-tenant keys only.",
  "cutoff_contract": "Retains PostgreSQL english full-text retrieval, rank and kinds. A cutoff now excludes both later-created and later-updated chunks, with disjoint creation/update and total counts; cannot reconstruct old edited text or full historical corpus. Missing-time actual-table fixture prohibited by original NOT NULL, covered by unit/projection only.",
  "adoption_contract": "Typed status/reason/HTTP/cache/query/cutoff with tenant and row validation; identity/url/cutoff/query cache, no stale failed-refresh adoption. Budgeted/sanitized rows and resolvable marker table are exactly the adopted subset. Exact nonce block/hash and actual/invalid model citations are recorded; providing material does not establish accuracy or citation quality.",
  "containment_contract": "KB inline boundary note compressed equivalently after actual8717/8105 pre-model budget failures; full safety meanings retained, shared standing system/registry/8000cap unchanged. Shared envelope module unchanged. KB-specific preparation preserves guard scanning, field sanitization, nonce stripping, untrusted tags and nonce fence while budgeting encoded Unicode/escape length before a single rendering to avoid hidden second truncation.",
  "persistence_contract": "knowledge_base_read is part of original verdict transaction and guarded first-write artifact. Artifact failure rolls back, retry does not duplicate; generic Run/alert retry updates remain unchanged.",
  "fixture_contract": "Six marked synthetic documents reuse A/B test tenants. Actual Fusion-derived query is checked before one model call; only new A/B runbook text/title may receive explicitly synthetic test retrieval terms or compact lexical terms/minimalSOP, recording old/new hash and updated_at after cutoff tests. No claim of actual tenant SOP, authoring/ingest or vector quality.",
  "scope_limitations": [
    "Default120-second cache does not instantly observe server-side revocation/edit/deletion. Mapping is read before cache.",
    "Recent dispositions and identity readers remain separate work; resident worker/graph/approvals/responses stay disabled.",
    "One actual model example does not accept full retrieval/citation/classification or server quality."
  ]
